            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all four changed paths in full. The change adds EncodeExemption/DecodeExemption and ExemptionHandoff, and refactors EncodeResult/DecodeResult through shared encodeFile/decodeFile helpers.",
              "Input handling: DecodeExemption goes through decodeFile, which rejects duplicate keys and unknown members with jsonstrict, then checks version, risk and report. All failures wrap ErrInvalidStored, and the zero value is returned on refusal. EncodeExemption refuses a non-JSON report before writing anything. I found no unsafe input path.",
              "Refactor equivalence: the DecodeResult and EncodeResult behavior is preserved (same strict checks, same error wrapping, same encoder settings). The only change is that the error text for encode failures now uses a parameterized name, which is not a security impact.",
              "Data exposure: no secrets, network access, filesystem access, or dependency changes are introduced. The stored file holds only the binding, a risk declaration and the verifier report, all of which are caller-supplied.",
              "No backend authorization or enforcement surface is touched. ExemptionHandoff only builds a skeleton record, and the engine's roles parsing validates the parent-filled fields, as the tests show.",
              "No reachable exploit or scanner evidence was found, so no findings are reported."
            ]
          }
        }
