            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The EncodeResult refactor into bindingOf and encodeFile keeps the same encoder settings: indent, no HTML escaping, and a trailing newline. The error text changes only by the what parameter, which is 'result' for results, so it reads as before.",
              "DecodeResult now goes through decodeFile and keeps the same version and reply checks and the same ErrInvalidStored wrapping. An exemption file carries risk and report members, which a result does not have, so strict decoding should refuse it. TestDecodeResultRefusesTheFileOfAnExemption covers this.",
              "DecodeExemption refuses duplicate keys, unknown members, other versions, an empty risk, and a missing or null report. It returns the zero value on refusal. The table-driven test asserts both the error class and the zero value for each case.",
              "EncodeExemption refuses a report that is not valid JSON and wraps ErrReplyNotJSON. The test covers an empty string, prose and truncated JSON.",
              "ExemptionHandoff reuses Handoff and overrides ToRole, PayloadKind and Evidence[1].Kind. This depends on Handoff returning two evidence entries, which I cannot see in this patch. The new test asserts the exact evidence slice, so a regression there would be caught.",
              "Minor gap, not a defect: DecodeExemption does not require the binding member to be present, so a file with no binding decodes to an empty binding. The later binding comparison would reject it, so this is not a reliability failure."
            ]
          }
        }
